                            ProblemStatement = "Priya in Finance says invoices from a supplier at billing@northwind-supply.example have stopped reaching her. Internal email works, and she has checked her Junk Email folder. The supplier received no bounce message.",
                            TechnicalExplanation = "Message trace is the starting point for any 'where did my email go?' ticket because it shows what Exchange Online actually did with the message. A Quarantined status means Microsoft Defender for Office 365 or Exchange Online Protection held the message before it reached the mailbox, which is why it was not in Junk and why the sender got no bounce. After releasing it, report the false positive through Submissions and let Microsoft create the Tenant Allow/Block List entry. That keeps the exception narrow and time-limited, whereas a domain on the anti-spam allowed list skips spam filtering for anyone spoofing that domain.",
